        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying Ensure Plus for a Healthy Weight</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Ensure Plus and Ensure Max Protein look alike on the shelf, but Plus delivers 350 calories and 19 g of sugar for 16 g of protein. For an older adult with a stable weight who just needs more protein, that adds calories and sugar without much benefit. Check the protein and calorie lines before buying a case.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating Weight Loss as Good News</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                When an older adult loses weight without trying, swapping meals for a 150-calorie lean shake can make it worse. Unexplained weight loss deserves a doctor's visit, and the drink should usually be a calorie-dense one such as Ensure Plus or BOOST Very High Calorie, chosen with a dietitian where possible.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring Kidney Function</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Adding 30 g of protein a day is fine for most seniors but not for someone with advanced kidney disease who is not on dialysis. Kidney function often declines quietly with age and diabetes, so ask the doctor about recent eGFR results before starting a daily high-protein drink.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Starting a Shake Without Telling the Warfarin Clinic</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Many shakes contain added vitamin K, some at half the daily value per bottle. People on warfarin can usually still drink them, but the intake has to be steady and the anticoagulation clinic needs to know. Starting or stopping a daily shake without a word can push INR results out of range.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting the Shake to Do the Exercise's Job</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Protein alone does little to rebuild lost strength. The research behind the 1.0 to 1.2 g/kg target pairs it with regular activity and resistance exercise. A shake plus a simple, approved strength routine, two or three times a week, is what actually protects muscle in later life.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

